loom qa runner=83 witness_rye=100
file glow/*_witness.rye and glow/nock/*_witness.rye the comptime declaration walker in 63 files, each naming its own subject identifier, each built
file tools/fixtures/r/rye_witness_walker_scan.sh ceiling 119 -> 56, with the lane and the remainder named in the comment that carries it
file tools/n/nock_glow_mirror_witness.rish the runner the seam's first pin never had; builds, runs, and asserts four of its printed claims
file glow/nock/nock_glow_mirror_witness.rye the self-path in its own header corrected from nock/ to glow/nock/
file construction/REDS.md %504 booked BOOKED with the measurement; %463 closed on metal and folded
file construction/archive/REDS-the-tree-a-census-is-easiest-to-test-on-rows-463.md the shelf, holding the census numbers because the numbers are the finding
file construction/ITINERARY.md the live front, with two of my own shelf pointers merged into one so the card stayed under bound
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md the cairn for that merge, naming why a merge is a fold rather than a trim
recommend check-in (Claude) -- the lane's own sweep is done and measured, and what it turned up wants a ruling rather than a lap. %504's remainder is one predicate: rye_compile_reach_scan derives asserted from runner mentions alone, and widening it to living Markdown re-grades the whole never set in one step, which is the same reason %496 held its link density back. That is a seat, not a mechanical lap. The 56 unwalked that remain are linengrow (51), mand (3), mantra (1) and tools/rye (1) -- other lanes, each four lines from the same proof, and a claim-as-override would take them if you want the ratchet at zero. My own next honest lap is the helper hazard I declined today: the walker census reads one literal spelling, so the first lap that factors those four lines into a shared function will silently un-walk everything it touches.
